                <pb facs="0959" n="899" sameAs="frus:frus1868p2/pg899"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Translation.]</seg></opener>
                <head>Señor Garcia to Mr. Seward.</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Clarendon Hotel,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">New York,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1868-04-29"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >April</hi> 29, 1868.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> I have had the honor to receive your
                    excellency’s note of yesterday, inclosing the reply of your department to a note
                    of Mr. Ignacio Gomez, the Nicaragua plenipotentiary, communicating to your
                    excellency the offer of his government to intercede between the allied republics
                    and Spain to effect a permanent peace.</p>
                <p>The sincere and friendly interest which your excellency has ever shown for the
                    conclusion of that war, and which you repeat in your reply, will be highly
                    appreciated by my government.</p>
                <p>On renewing to your excellency the assurances of my personal consideration, I
                    subscribe myself your attentive servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>JOSÉ ANTONIO G. Y GAECIA.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p>Hon. <hi rendition="#small-caps">William</hi> H. <hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Seward</hi><hi rendition="#italic">, &amp;c<hi rendition="#italic">.,
                                &amp;</hi>c<hi rendition="#italic">.,</hi> &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
